    "scope_review": {
      "HilbertGramReciprocity": "Actual complete RCLike Hilbert spaces and native eigenspaces. Positivity uses a nonzero eigenvector from HasEigenvalue. The native LinearIsometryEquiv is constructed from the prior Gram equivalence and proven inner-product preservation. Positive parameter may have zero eigenspaces; no existence or spectral-completeness conclusion is inferred from the construction alone.",
      "HilbertGramMoorePenrose": "Typed rectangular continuous-map compositions remain ordered. BAA* = A* uses precisely ABA=A and self-adjoint BA. General reciprocal action consumes the four-equation native repo predicate; the closed-range specializations consume the existing constructed bounded map. Norm cancellation uses an actual nonzero eigenvector. The final quantified small-positive-eigenvalue criterion is one-way and has no eigenbasis, Fredholm, or unbounded inverse conclusion.",
      "GradedExponentialTrace": "General ring cancellation is reused with characteristic-zero scalar output. The generic analytic theorem requires a complete normed algebra and a continuous linear cyclic functional, and transports an actual native HasSum. Matrix specialization uses arbitrary rectangular factors, doubled blocks, and native continuous trace; empty index types remain allowed. The separate commutator-exponential cancellation only needs square-zero E, an additive cyclic functional, and native exponential commutation, with completeness explicitly omitted. The 2x2 witness proves genuine noncommutation and separates the exponential weight from the finite EF weight."
    },
